1. AGREEMENT

This End User License Agreement ("Agreement") is a legal agreement between you ("Licensee") and VerdantStack ("Licensor") for the use of the SvelteKit + Postgres Starter software package ("Software").

By purchasing or using the Software, you agree to be bound by the terms of this Agreement.

2. GRANT OF LICENSE

Subject to the terms of this Agreement, Licensor grants you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, single-seat license to:

  - Use the Software in production environments
  - Modify the Software for your own projects
  - Create derivative works based on the Software

This license covers an unlimited number of your own projects — one licensed developer may build and ship as many end products as they like.

3. RESTRICTIONS

You may NOT:

  - Resell, sublicense, or distribute the Software to third parties
  - Share your license key or access credentials with others
  - Use the Software with multiple developers without purchasing additional licenses (licenses are per developer, not per project)
  - Remove or alter any copyright notices or license terms
  - Claim authorship of the original Software
  - Resell or redistribute the Software, or build a competing starter kit / boilerplate product from it (building your own end product is always allowed)

4. SEATS AND LICENCES

Each licence is per developer, not per project.

- Licence: Seats / Projects / Notes
- Individual: 1 / Unlimited / The standard licence.
- Team: 3 or more / Unlimited / Covers every developer on the team, not per-project.

  - Individual Licence: one developer, unlimited projects.
  - Team Licence: covers three or more developers who work on the same
product or client engagement. Additional seats are added to the same
licence at the per-seat rate shown on the product page at time of purchase.
  - A Team Licence is priced per team, and its price is listed on the product
page. It is not sold as "available upon request" — a prospect who cannot
see a price cannot budget for it, and a tier that requires a conversation
before it can be quoted is a tier that loses the buyer who is willing to
decide today.

> Changed in 1.4. Version 1.3 said "Team License: Available upon request".
> That was an unpriced promise: the licence already granted unlimited
> projects, but the one thing a paid licence exists to buy — a second pair of
> hands — had no price. The tier is now defined, with its terms binding.

