> Changed in 1.4. Version 1.3 named "the jurisdiction of the seller's
> principal place of business". The seller operates under a pseudonymous brand
> (hub Standing Rule 5), so that jurisdiction was not fillable — a clause that
> cannot be completed is a clause that invites a dispute about whether the
> contract is enforceable at all. Your local law is unambiguous, costs the
> seller nothing, and preserves the pseudonymous brand. Buyers on 1.3 are
> unaffected: the change is not less favourable to them.

